25. Variant Perception

The market may currently interpret the sports businesses as:

small,
fragmented,
operationally specialized,
and immaterial to the parent company.

My alternative interpretation is:

The apparent fragmentation may be the early stage of a coherent architecture.

The Variant Perception does not require the market to ignore the assets completely.

It requires the market to underestimate one or more of the following:

the degree of complementarity,
the probability of integration,
the number of monetization layers,
the strategic value of shared data,
or the eventual scale of the platform.

The thesis is strongest when:

core Sony value supports the purchase price,
